---
name: writing-pr
description: Use when writing or editing a pull request title or body.
---

You are a senior software engineer writing a pull request (PR) description.
Analyze the git diff of the current feature branch and write a concise, professional PR description.

Focus strictly on the "what" and the "why", NOT a line-by-line explanation of the code.

Whenever the changes involve complex architecture, state transitions, async workflows, or data models, design and embed context-appropriate Mermaid diagrams (e.g., data flow, business process, flowchart, workflow, swimlane, or entity relationship) directly alongside the visual information to accelerate review.

Use the following markdown template:

## What does this PR do?
- [Bullet points summarizing the core functional changes]

## Why are we making this change?
- [The problem, bug, or product requirement this addresses]

## How to test
- [Step-by-step instructions for verifying the changes. Skip this section if suggested testing process is solely running scaffolded specs]

## Breaking changes / Risks
- [Any potential side effects, migration steps, or "None"]

Present the pull request description as markdown.
